WEBVTT

00:00:00.638 --> 00:00:04.975
Welcome to Dial Captain This guide takes you through installation

00:00:04.888 --> 00:00:08.288
and setup one step at a time We will connect

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.538
the small controller to Wi-Fi pair a Philips Hue Tap

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:15.538
Dial and configure Roon Blu OS or WiiM You do

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.288
not need programming knowledge Pause whenever you want to follow

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.375
a step at your own pace The chapters below the

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:25.038
video let you jump straight to the mode you want

00:00:26.971 --> 00:00:30.421
The Tap Dial sends button presses and dial movements to

00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:35.108
the ESP over Zigbee The ESP translates them into Wi-Fi

00:00:35.021 --> 00:00:38.833
control commands Exactly one mode is active at a time

00:00:39.108 --> 00:00:43.233
Roon Blu OS or WiiM Settings for the other modes

00:00:43.146 --> 00:00:47.096
are retained Dial Captain does not stream music or act

00:00:47.008 --> 00:00:49.883
as a speaker You do not need a Hue Bridge

00:00:50.046 --> 00:00:54.171
Roon Pilot or an additional computer service Roon mode still

00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:56.296
requires your existing Roon Server

00:00:58.221 --> 00:01:02.596
Prepare an ESP32 C6 Zero with eight megabytes of flash

00:01:02.821 --> 00:01:07.121
a Philips Hue Tap Dial model RDM002 and a USB

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:12.496
data cable Check the exact board name A similar-looking ESP32

00:01:12.408 --> 00:01:16.196
S3 is not the same device The Tap Dial runs

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:21.308
on its battery The ESP however needs continuous USB power

00:01:21.608 --> 00:01:24.058
You will also need the name and password of your

00:01:23.971 --> 00:01:29.733
2.4 gigahertz Wi-Fi network A charge-only USB cable cannot transfer

00:01:29.646 --> 00:01:30.371
firmware

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:36.292
Open Chrome or Edge on your computer This guide uses

00:01:36.204 --> 00:01:39.804
the tested USB workflow in those browsers it does not

00:01:39.717 --> 00:01:43.792
cover installation on a phone Close serial monitors and other

00:01:43.704 --> 00:01:48.817
browser tabs already using the ESP Your computer ESP and

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:50.992
player must be able to reach each other on the

00:01:50.904 --> 00:01:56.392
home network An isolated guest network is unsuitable Later you

00:01:56.304 --> 00:01:59.392
can open the device configuration from a phone on that

00:01:59.304 --> 00:02:00.067
network

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:06.000
A factory-new ESP has nothing to back up If Dial

00:02:05.912 --> 00:02:09.662
Captain is already configured first export its settings from the

00:02:09.575 --> 00:02:14.462
device webpage or USB assistant A complete erase also removes

00:02:14.375 --> 00:02:19.212
Wi-Fi button assignments and Tap Dial pairing The backup belongs

00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:23.725
to that particular ESP and contains private credentials Keep it

00:02:23.638 --> 00:02:28.225
on your computer We will cover restoration later A firmware

00:02:28.138 --> 00:02:31.187
update is no reason to reset the Tap Dial as

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.000
a precaution

00:02:33.917 --> 00:02:37.867
Start on the Dial Captain project website hosted on GitHub

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:41.854
It provides the guide and the entry for USB installation

00:02:42.154 --> 00:02:45.217
At the time of this video a public firmware release

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:48.854
and online installer have not yet been approved The following

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:52.542
recordings show the existing local development installer so you can

00:02:52.454 --> 00:02:56.304
learn the workflow A status page is not an installation

00:02:56.217 --> 00:03:00.304
error Once the public installer is released start from the

00:03:00.217 --> 00:03:04.504
project page This video does not publish firmware itself

00:03:06.392 --> 00:03:10.967
Connect only the intended ESP32 C6 to your computer by

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:15.979
USB Temporarily disconnect other ESP boards from the computer to

00:03:15.892 --> 00:03:19.467
avoid selecting the wrong one If you have trouble use

00:03:19.379 --> 00:03:22.904
a direct USB port rather than a hub Locate the

00:03:22.817 --> 00:03:26.767
small BOOT and RESET buttons on your board Their positions

00:03:26.679 --> 00:03:30.804
can vary between board versions The illustration explains their

00:03:30.717 --> 00:03:33.467
functions and is not a scale drawing of the board

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.092
layout

00:03:36.012 --> 00:03:40.412
The first installation may require manual download mode Leave the

00:03:40.325 --> 00:03:45.950
ESP connected by USB Hold BOOT While holding it briefly

00:03:45.862 --> 00:03:50.662
press and release RESET Then release BOOT Open the browser

00:03:50.575 --> 00:03:55.038
USB selection again Do not press either button while firmware

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.938
is being written Unlike the round Roon Pilot this separate

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:02.475
C6 board does not select a second processor by reversing

00:04:02.388 --> 00:04:03.725
the USB connector

00:04:05.654 --> 00:04:10.117
In the local installer select Install or update firmware The

00:04:10.029 --> 00:04:14.529
browser opens its own device picker Click the connected ESP

00:04:14.442 --> 00:04:18.767
and then Connect It is often called USB JTAG or

00:04:18.679 --> 00:04:22.517
Serial Debug Unit On Windows it may include a COM

00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:25.942
number On macOS the name looks different and there is

00:04:25.854 --> 00:04:29.492
no Windows COM number Names and numbers in this video

00:04:29.404 --> 00:04:33.729
are examples If unsure cancel and unplug the board to

00:04:33.642 --> 00:04:35.292
see which entry disappears

00:04:37.221 --> 00:04:42.446
After USB access is granted the installation dialog appears Choose

00:04:42.358 --> 00:04:46.721
Install Dial Captain The name and displayed version must match

00:04:46.633 --> 00:04:51.683
your intended device The installer is configured for the ESP32

00:04:51.596 --> 00:04:55.171
C6 If another chip is reported or the board is

00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:59.933
unsupported do not install unrelated firmware Close the dialog and

00:04:59.846 --> 00:05:04.271
check the board cable and selected USB port first These

00:05:04.183 --> 00:05:08.033
installer dialogs may use English labels even when the surrounding

00:05:07.946 --> 00:05:09.071
page is German

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:15.750
For a clean installation select Erase device then Next This

00:05:15.662 --> 00:05:20.100
removes existing data on the ESP including saved Wi-Fi and

00:05:20.012 --> 00:05:23.400
Tap Dial pairing data On a new board it gives

00:05:23.312 --> 00:05:27.238
you a clean starting point On an existing device make

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:30.938
sure you already have your backup file An appropriate update

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:34.013
without erasing can retain settings but that is not a

00:05:33.925 --> 00:05:37.700
blanket guarantee for every firmware version and storage layout

00:05:39.612 --> 00:05:43.550
Read the final confirmation Check once more that you intend

00:05:43.462 --> 00:05:47.538
to install Dial Captain on the correct C6 board Only

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:52.412
then click Install Keep the USB cable connected throughout Do

00:05:52.325 --> 00:05:55.562
not close the browser window or let the computer sleep

00:05:55.862 --> 00:05:59.213
The progress shown in the video is shortened You do

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:03.150
not need to select individual files enter memory addresses or

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.138
install a development environment

00:06:07.096 --> 00:06:11.221
The installer prepares the board erases storage if requested and

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:14.733
writes the firmware The percentage can pause for a while

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:19.196
Wait for the explicit completion message Reaching one hundred

00:06:19.108 --> 00:06:22.408
percent alone is not a reason to unplug If the

00:06:22.321 --> 00:06:26.471
browser reports an error record its exact text Check the

00:06:26.383 --> 00:06:30.958
cable direct USB connection and download mode before trying again

00:06:31.233 --> 00:06:34.658
A video animation is of course not proof of a

00:06:34.571 --> 00:06:36.096
physical flashing test

00:06:37.988 --> 00:06:42.588
After successful completion close the installation dialog This

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.450
releases the USB port for the next step BOOT must

00:06:46.362 --> 00:06:49.988
now be released If the board remains in download mode

00:06:50.188 --> 00:06:54.188
briefly press RESET without holding BOOT Wait a moment for

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:58.188
the new firmware to start The USB entry may disappear

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:01.988
briefly and return You do not need a separate application

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.812
to configure Wi-Fi first

00:07:05.683 --> 00:07:10.308
Below the installer click Start setup Select the same ESP

00:07:10.221 --> 00:07:14.308
again in the USB picker and confirm This is intentional

00:07:14.508 --> 00:07:17.508
the installer used the port first and now the setup

00:07:17.421 --> 00:07:20.708
assistant talks to the running firmware If the port is

00:07:20.621 --> 00:07:24.308
busy check whether the old installation dialog or a serial

00:07:24.221 --> 00:07:28.021
monitor is still open The ESP does not need Wi-Fi

00:07:27.933 --> 00:07:30.583
yet and you do not need to select a special

00:07:30.496 --> 00:07:32.358
setup network on your computer

00:07:34.304 --> 00:07:38.092
You now have two choices For the first setup choose

00:07:38.004 --> 00:07:40.704
Set up as new If you have a backup from

00:07:40.617 --> 00:07:44.729
this exact ESP you can instead choose Restore backup even

00:07:44.642 --> 00:07:48.617
before Wi-Fi is configured We will follow new setup first

00:07:48.529 --> 00:07:52.117
and cover restoration in its own chapter A backup from

00:07:52.029 --> 00:07:54.742
another ESP is not a way to clone a second

00:07:54.654 --> 00:07:57.767
controller or pair one Tap Dial to two devices at

00:07:57.679 --> 00:07:58.617
the same time

00:08:00.554 --> 00:08:03.829
The assistant searches for Wi-Fi networks within range of the

00:08:03.742 --> 00:08:07.542
ESP Open the list and choose your own 2.4 gigahertz

00:08:07.454 --> 00:08:11.129
network Do not confuse it with a neighbour’s similar name

00:08:11.042 --> 00:08:15.117
or an isolated guest network If yours is missing scan

00:08:15.029 --> 00:08:19.217
again or enter its exact name manually Your computer stays

00:08:19.129 --> 00:08:23.092
on its normal home network Dial Captain does not create

00:08:23.004 --> 00:08:26.742
a setup hotspot for this workflow The details are sent

00:08:26.654 --> 00:08:29.429
directly to the ESP over USB

00:08:31.321 --> 00:08:36.433
Enter your Wi-Fi password This video uses fictional example details

00:08:36.346 --> 00:08:40.371
only If needed use Show to check for typing mistakes

00:08:40.533 --> 00:08:44.771
then hide the password again Select Test connection and save

00:08:45.046 --> 00:08:49.358
New credentials are saved only after a successful connection If

00:08:49.271 --> 00:08:53.758
the test fails check the name password and 2.4 gigahertz

00:08:53.671 --> 00:08:58.196
network An unsuccessful attempt does not replace previously saved

00:08:58.108 --> 00:08:59.058
credentials

00:09:01.012 --> 00:09:04.375
Once Wi-Fi is connected you can choose a Roon Server

00:09:04.288 --> 00:09:08.512
or open the device webpage directly Blu OS and WiiM

00:09:08.425 --> 00:09:11.288
need no approval in Roon so you can skip server

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:15.675
selection Note the device address shown by the assistant Your

00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:18.925
router assigns it and yours will differ from the video

00:09:18.838 --> 00:09:24.113
example The address 192 dot 168 dot 4 dot 1

00:09:24.025 --> 00:09:26.650
used in some other device guides is not used for

00:09:26.562 --> 00:09:27.912
this USB setup

00:09:29.821 --> 00:09:34.533
In the assistant choose Enable web configuration Once the service

00:09:34.446 --> 00:09:39.246
is ready Open web configuration appears Click it The new

00:09:39.158 --> 00:09:42.571
tab shows a webpage served by the ESP not a

00:09:42.483 --> 00:09:46.858
cloud configuration service Your computer or phone must be able

00:09:46.771 --> 00:09:50.133
to reach that ESP on the home network While the

00:09:50.046 --> 00:09:53.858
web server is active the board’s RGB LED gently blinks

00:09:53.771 --> 00:09:57.683
amber This works even before any Tap Dial is paired

00:09:57.596 --> 00:09:59.533
or any Roon Server selected

00:10:01.458 --> 00:10:05.158
Find the Pair Philips Hue Tap Dial section A new

00:10:05.071 --> 00:10:09.283
device has no controller assigned yet Click Pair your first

00:10:09.196 --> 00:10:13.796
Tap Dial Discovery is now open for three minutes Place

00:10:13.708 --> 00:10:17.346
the intended Tap Dial near the ESP You do not

00:10:17.258 --> 00:10:20.071
need a Hue Bridge or an already paired controller for

00:10:19.983 --> 00:10:24.546
this Simply powering the ESP does not leave pairing permanently

00:10:24.458 --> 00:10:27.821
open You deliberately start discovery here

00:10:29.762 --> 00:10:32.425
On a new Tap Dial hold the button marked with

00:10:32.338 --> 00:10:35.575
one dot for about three seconds until its LED blinks

00:10:35.875 --> 00:10:39.462
The browser should progress from Searching to Checking and Setting

00:10:39.375 --> 00:10:43.613
up During setup briefly press a button occasionally to keep

00:10:43.525 --> 00:10:47.838
the battery-powered controller awake These presses do not send music

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:51.562
commands while pairing is in progress If your Tap Dial

00:10:51.475 --> 00:10:55.088
already belongs to a Hue Bridge or another ESP follow

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.338
the next step first

00:10:58.262 --> 00:11:01.625
A Tap Dial can belong to only one Zigbee network

00:11:01.925 --> 00:11:04.200
If it was paired with a Hue Bridge or another

00:11:04.112 --> 00:11:08.325
ESP reset that controller only hold SETUP on its back

00:11:08.238 --> 00:11:11.988
for more than ten seconds This removes its old pairing

00:11:12.288 --> 00:11:16.625
Then with discovery open use button one again Do not

00:11:16.538 --> 00:11:21.300
factory-reset the ESP for this When restoring a suitable backup

00:11:21.212 --> 00:11:24.562
to the same ESP resetting the controller is not the

00:11:24.475 --> 00:11:25.562
normal procedure

00:11:27.512 --> 00:11:30.800
Wait until the page says Done Only then is the

00:11:30.712 --> 00:11:35.512
assignment saved The progress states shown demonstrate the interface

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:38.850
Full first pairing of a new controller has not yet

00:11:38.762 --> 00:11:43.075
completed physical acceptance in this development version Use Set up

00:11:42.988 --> 00:11:47.275
again for the existing controller A different Tap Dial replaces

00:11:47.188 --> 00:11:52.288
it only after successful confirmed setup Cancelling or timing out

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:55.962
does not delete the previous assignment Check the battery and

00:11:55.875 --> 00:11:58.788
keep the controller awake before resetting anything

00:12:00.708 --> 00:12:04.696
Under Mode choose what the Tap Dial should control Roon

00:12:04.608 --> 00:12:08.633
controls a zone on your Roon Server Blu OS controls

00:12:08.546 --> 00:12:13.083
a Blu OS player directly WiiM controls a WiiM directly

00:12:12.996 --> 00:12:16.521
through its local interface Only one mode runs at a

00:12:16.433 --> 00:12:20.533
time Saving activates your choice without deleting the other

00:12:20.446 --> 00:12:25.121
profiles The next chapters cover all three paths You only

00:12:25.033 --> 00:12:27.733
need to configure the one you intend to use now

00:12:29.667 --> 00:12:33.154
For Roon select Roon mode on the device webpage and

00:12:33.067 --> 00:12:38.242
save In the USB assistant open Roon Server selection Choose

00:12:38.154 --> 00:12:41.392
your running server from the list and save it If

00:12:41.304 --> 00:12:44.729
discovery is empty first check that the server is running

00:12:44.642 --> 00:12:48.917
and reachable on your network Alternatively check its address with

00:12:48.829 --> 00:12:54.029
the usual API port 9330 Avoid selecting a second server

00:12:53.942 --> 00:12:57.717
by mistake A different server needs its own approval and

00:12:57.629 --> 00:12:58.992
a new zone selection

00:13:00.904 --> 00:13:06.242
Now open Roon then Settings and Extensions Find Dial Captain

00:13:06.154 --> 00:13:11.092
and click Enable Next open the extension’s settings cog This

00:13:11.004 --> 00:13:15.104
schematic view explains the path the exact arrangement can vary

00:13:15.017 --> 00:13:18.617
with your Roon version Use Check connection in the USB

00:13:18.529 --> 00:13:22.879
assistant to see whether approval has arrived Configure Roon volume

00:13:22.792 --> 00:13:25.829
and buttons in that settings cog rather than on the

00:13:25.742 --> 00:13:27.304
general device webpage

00:13:29.183 --> 00:13:33.271
Choose your Roon zone Set the extension language to German

00:13:33.183 --> 00:13:36.158
or English as needed it is independent of the Roon

00:13:36.071 --> 00:13:40.746
app language Sensitivity and Steps per click are separate settings

00:13:41.046 --> 00:13:44.533
You can select one to four native Roon steps With

00:13:44.446 --> 00:13:47.933
an output using half a decibel per step two steps

00:13:47.846 --> 00:13:51.058
give one decibel per click Each of the four buttons

00:13:50.971 --> 00:13:53.783
can have a short and long action such as play

00:13:53.908 --> 00:13:56.658
pause next previous or mute

00:13:58.583 --> 00:14:02.108
For each of the three favourites first choose Roon playlist

00:14:02.021 --> 00:14:05.096
or Roon radio station then select an item from the

00:14:05.008 --> 00:14:09.433
list Radio stations come from My Live Radio You can

00:14:09.346 --> 00:14:13.546
page through longer lists Assign the favourites to buttons and

00:14:13.458 --> 00:14:17.833
save everything At low listening volume test one button press

00:14:17.746 --> 00:14:21.296
and a small dial movement first After the Tap Dial

00:14:21.208 --> 00:14:24.508
reports back its battery level can also appear in the

00:14:24.421 --> 00:14:28.396
status line A fixed Roon output may not support volume

00:14:28.308 --> 00:14:29.108
changes

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.312
For a Blu OS player choose Blu OS control on

00:14:34.225 --> 00:14:38.850
the device webpage Discovery shows reachable devices with their name

00:14:39.025 --> 00:14:43.500
model and address Deliberately select your player If it is

00:14:43.412 --> 00:14:47.938
missing enter the address manually the usual port is 11000

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:51.825
Check player and load presets confirms the target and loads

00:14:51.738 --> 00:14:56.162
its saved presets This does not start music The mode

00:14:56.075 --> 00:14:59.550
is for Blu OS generally not just one particular NODE

00:14:59.462 --> 00:14:59.988
model

00:15:01.917 --> 00:15:05.679
First save your radio stations or playlists as presets in

00:15:05.592 --> 00:15:09.129
the Blu OS app. Choose three of those as favourites

00:15:09.042 --> 00:15:13.767
here Assign short and long button actions then select sensitivity

00:15:13.679 --> 00:15:17.317
and half one or two decibels per click Save the

00:15:17.229 --> 00:15:21.017
settings With a fixed output level the ring has no

00:15:20.929 --> 00:15:25.554
effect Next and previous depend on the current source Dial

00:15:25.467 --> 00:15:28.979
Captain does not maintain its own streaming library and its

00:15:28.892 --> 00:15:32.529
volume commands do not explicitly adjust other group members

00:15:34.458 --> 00:15:38.408
For WiiM first save the desired content as presets in

00:15:38.321 --> 00:15:42.596
WiiM Home On the device webpage choose WiiM control and

00:15:42.508 --> 00:15:46.796
select the discovered player Alternatively enter its address the

00:15:46.708 --> 00:15:52.733
local HTTPS interface normally uses port 443 Check the player

00:15:52.646 --> 00:15:56.083
and load its presets Up to twelve entries can be

00:15:55.996 --> 00:15:59.433
shown Choose three as your favourites and assign them to

00:15:59.346 --> 00:16:03.946
short or long presses Supported content and track commands depend

00:16:03.858 --> 00:16:05.333
on the service and source

00:16:07.262 --> 00:16:10.488
On a new profile ring control of the WiiM’s own

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:14.100
volume starts disabled Enable it only if that is the

00:16:14.012 --> 00:16:18.162
volume you intend to control Choose one two or five

00:16:18.075 --> 00:16:22.362
percentage points per click then save This does not directly

00:16:22.275 --> 00:16:26.250
adjust an external DAC For a Roon zone using an

00:16:26.162 --> 00:16:31.087
RME volume provider use Roon mode The output configuration in

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:35.500
WiiM Home is not changed automatically Also note that WiiM

00:16:35.412 --> 00:16:38.550
mute commands can affect members of an existing group

00:16:40.471 --> 00:16:44.071
In daily use the web server is normally closed By

00:16:43.983 --> 00:16:47.308
default hold Tap Dial button four for at least eight

00:16:47.221 --> 00:16:52.133
seconds then release The amber LED indicates that configuration is

00:16:52.046 --> 00:16:56.208
available The same extra-long press closes it again without

00:16:56.121 --> 00:17:00.296
triggering an ordinary button action Alternatively hold BOOT on the

00:17:00.208 --> 00:17:04.496
running ESP for three seconds without pressing RESET or open

00:17:04.408 --> 00:17:09.421
access over USB After ten minutes without interaction the webpage

00:17:09.333 --> 00:17:15.146
closes Extend gives you another ten minutes Audio control continues

00:17:17.058 --> 00:17:21.796
Open Backup and restore then choose Export settings Your browser

00:17:21.708 --> 00:17:25.771
saves a JSON file on your computer It includes Wi-Fi

00:17:25.883 --> 00:17:29.708
Roon approval and zone buttons and favourites all Blu OS

00:17:29.621 --> 00:17:33.096
and WiiM profiles plus Tap Dial and Zigbee data for

00:17:33.008 --> 00:17:36.921
the same ESP Unsaved form edits are not exported No

00:17:36.833 --> 00:17:41.083
extra password or cloud account is required Because the file

00:17:40.996 --> 00:17:44.946
contains credentials do not attach it to public bug reports

00:17:45.208 --> 00:17:48.833
Export it before a complete USB reinstallation

00:17:50.762 --> 00:17:55.562
After reinstalling close the installer start USB setup and choose

00:17:55.475 --> 00:17:59.688
Restore backup Use the file from this exact ESP Check

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:04.050
the summary Explicit confirmation and preparation save the restore

00:18:03.962 --> 00:18:09.275
request Then choose Restart now and keep power connected Reconnect

00:18:09.188 --> 00:18:14.050
USB afterwards if needed Full restoration after a real factory

00:18:13.962 --> 00:18:17.938
flash has not yet completed physical acceptance in this development

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:22.050
version The film explains the workflow available in the assistant

00:18:22.262 --> 00:18:24.225
rather than claiming release approval

00:18:26.125 --> 00:18:29.925
After setup you no longer need the computer Power the

00:18:29.838 --> 00:18:33.550
ESP from a suitable USB supply and leave it connected

00:18:33.462 --> 00:18:37.362
to Wi-Fi The Tap Dial continues to use its battery

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:40.925
Roon still needs a running Roon Server Blu OS and

00:18:40.838 --> 00:18:45.262
WiiM are controlled directly A closed configuration webpage is

00:18:45.175 --> 00:18:48.500
normal and does not mean the controller is offline There

00:18:48.412 --> 00:18:53.700
is no dedicated over-the-air updater Future firmware updates use USB

00:18:53.612 --> 00:18:55.812
again so keep your backup file

00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:02.275
No USB device check the data cable direct port closed

00:19:02.188 --> 00:19:06.488
monitors and BOOT with RESET No Wi-Fi check the name

00:19:06.625 --> 00:19:12.038
password and 2.4 gigahertz network No device webpage enable the

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:15.875
temporary server first and use the actual IP address No

00:19:15.788 --> 00:19:19.875
music control check the active mode player or Roon zone

00:19:19.962 --> 00:19:24.425
and saved buttons No volume control check for fixed output

00:19:24.338 --> 00:19:28.188
and the WiiM ring option Record the version step and

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:32.362
exact message when reporting a fault Factory reset is not

00:19:32.275 --> 00:19:34.087
the first troubleshooting step

